+### Bot control-plane authentication
+
+Devin joins the member capability, dispatch, panel and worker-kit sets. Its
+host-derived `kirocrew-core`, `kirocrew-cron`, `kirocrew-dashboard` and
+`kirocrew-panel` elements use `acp/harness/devin_mcp.py`. The existing IPC issuer
+hands each its own one-time pickup, bound to this session's token and runtime
+pid; the wrapper redeems it and runs the ordinary server in the same process.
+No gateway secret is exposed and no third-party element gets a pickup. Other
+backends retain their existing issuance and launch behavior. Failed redemption
+never grants access. Per-tool-disabled servers remain withheld whole.
+
+The Bot harness picker/save validator and worker selector derive their entries
+from the capability sets, so a Devin pin uses the ordinary selection gate. This
+experimental integration is maintained as a downstream patch for reuse; it makes
+no claim of upstream support.
+
 ### Verification and keeping the patch separate
 
+`test/test_devin_saved_spec.py` verifies Bot selection, consumed saved-spec
+confirmation, edited-after-save refusal and worker projection.
+`test/test_devin_member_ipc_e2e.py` runs the real Bot MCP servers under Devin
+credential masking against an authenticated loopback gateway and verifies
+successful status and panel calls. `scripts/probe_devin_member.py` is an opt-in
+real Devin/AcpClient smoke with a disposable gateway/spec, real signed session
+identity, saved-spec confirmation, once-only approvals, shell rejection and
+resume. It uses existing Devin authentication and never edits the operator's
+Bot configuration. `scripts/drive_devin_gate.py` also uses a disposable config
+and worker echo server; only scenario-specific tool names are approved. Raw
+recordings stay private until their inputs and identifiers are reviewed.
+
 `test/test_acp_backend_devin.py` verifies the full-input permission envelope,
 allow-once/reject behavior, rejection of native bypass/persistent choices, missing
 hook and unasked-completion tripwires, package digests and project-config refusal.
